From e45b2cb6d7f3e8b1704a5b4ce35db11a55b0a8e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fluorite Integration Role
Date: Sun, 29 Mar 2026 22:15:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] flutter-auto: restore agl_shell binding for BG and panel
 views

Upstream-Status: Pending

Patch 0003 intentionally narrowed agl_shell binding so that the fluorite
NORMAL experiment could bind to agl_shell. That also removed the original
condition that bound agl_shell for non-NORMAL views.

As a result, helper clients started with `--window-type BG` or panel roles but
with an app id other than `fluorite` never bind to agl_shell. Their calls to
`agl_shell_set_background()` or `agl_shell_set_panel()` become no-ops, the
surface keeps role NONE, and the compositor leaves it in the pending list.

Keep the fluorite NORMAL special case, but restore the original non-NORMAL
binding rule so dedicated BG or panel helper clients can still claim their AGL
roles.
---
diff --git a/shell/wayland/display.cc b/shell/wayland/display.cc
--- a/shell/wayland/display.cc
+++ b/shell/wayland/display.cc
@@ -48,7 +48,9 @@ Display::Display(const bool enable_cursor,
   wayland_event_mask_update(ignore_wayland_event, m_wayland_event_mask);
 
   for (auto const& cfg : configs) {
-    if (cfg.app_id == "fluorite") {
+    if (cfg.app_id == "fluorite" ||
+        WaylandWindow::WINDOW_NORMAL !=
+            WaylandWindow::get_window_type(cfg.view.window_type)) {
       m_agl.bind_to_agl_shell = true;
       break;
     }
